## SPEC.md Updates

After completing a feature, update `docs/SPEC.md`. Trigger phrases:
- "feature complete", "update spec", "update documentation"
- "spec update", "document this feature"

**Update workflow:**
1. Review recent git changes (`git diff`, `git log`) to understand what was built
2. Update the relevant sections of `docs/SPEC.md`:
   - Add feature to "Implemented" section
   - Document key architectural decisions
   - Update "Current State" as needed
   - Add new entries to "Version History" table
3. Commit the SPEC update to the current branch

## Post-Implementation (Mandatory)

After completing all implementation stories and before claiming "done", run the post-implementation checklist (`post-implementation.mdc`) proactively. Do NOT wait for the user to ask. This includes: doc alignment, dead code scan, import consistency, and gitignore compliance.

## Multi-Phase Execution

When an implementation plan has multiple phases:

1. Create ONE plan covering all phases with a single todo list
2. Get user confirmation ONCE
3. Execute sequentially -- mark todos in_progress/completed as you go
4. At each phase boundary, run tests then immediately continue
5. Do NOT switch to plan mode between phases
6. Announce "Phase N complete (X tests pass). Continuing to Phase N+1." and keep going
7. Only pause if tests fail -- fix before proceeding

## Quality Enforcement

This project enforces quality through multiple mechanisms:

| Mechanism | Type | Purpose |
|-----------|------|---------|
| `context-management.mdc` | Always-applied rule | Session checkpoints, handoff, completion checks |
| `workflow.mdc` | Always-applied rule | Development workflow, branching, verification |
| `post-implementation.mdc` | Description-triggered rule | Doc alignment, dead code, import/gitignore checks after implementation |
| `pre-pr-review.mdc` | Description-triggered rule | Self-review: security, defensive coding, consistency before PR |
| `test-first.mdc` | Description-triggered rule | TDD workflow for new features |
| `design-review.mdc` | Description-triggered rule | UI/UX design review framework |
| `memory.mdc` | Description-triggered rule | Agent memory capture, load, and learning review |
| `.husky/pre-commit` | Git hook | Tests + lint + secrets check before commit, blocks main branch commits |
